  "face_shape_notes": "peak_position_adjustment_pct_points belongs to the face shape and is added to the peak_position_pct_from_head of the recommended and the alternate style alike. It does not apply to Straight, which has no peak position (null). For a plateau style, peak_plateau_range_pct moves with the centre figure by the same adjustment.",
  "peak_type_note": "peak_type is pointed, plateau or level. pointed: a single highest point. plateau: a flat run, where peak_position_pct_from_head is the centre of the run and peak_plateau_range_pct is its span; it is not a point to build toward. level: Straight, which has no peak. A style is plateau where the top edge falls by less than 0.04 eye width at 15 points of length either side of the peak, pointed where it falls by 0.06 or more.",
  "peak_position_range_note": "peak_position_range_pct is given only where peak position moves by more than 10 points with the edge setting: [low, high]. null means the figure is stable."
